'' A LINK WITH NOTHING NEW IS SKIPPED (tiko-build B5, RFC §6.4): the third build's objects are
'' the cache's, as the second's were, and the exe is as that link left it -- its record in the
'' module cache says so, and -v says the link is up to date. Nothing is left beside the exe.
'' The program still runs.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TIKO_MODCACHE=build/.blkc/cache
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' CLEAN: build/.blkc
'' CLEAN: build/.blk
'' COPY: tests/driver/src/unitcache => build/.blk/src
'' STEP: build -target windows-x86_64 build/.blk/src/a.tiko build/.blk/src/b.tiko -o build/.blk/app.exe
'' STEP: build -target windows-x86_64 build/.blk/src/a.tiko build/.blk/src/b.tiko -o build/.blk/app.exe
'' ARGS: build -target windows-x86_64 build/.blk/src/a.tiko build/.blk/src/b.tiko -o build/.blk/app.exe -v
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: link: build/.blk/app.exe is up to date
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.blkc/cache/links/*.link :: \nartifact 
'' EXPECT-NO-FILE: build/.blk/app.exe.link
'' RUN: build/.blk/app.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: b says 7
